# Typecheck (strict + noImplicitAny), prop-wiring check, the full test suite
# and the audit gate must pass before every commit. npm.cmd is not directly
# executable by sh on Windows, so everything runs through the async watchdog
# runner (scripts/quality-chain.mjs) — spawn-only, no shell strings, no
# execSync chains: a slow step is killed tree-wide on timeout instead of
# wedging the msys fork table (the documented reason commits used to need
# core.hooksPath=/dev/null, see DEVELOPMENT_HISTORY.md).
#
# The audit gate runs with a lockfile-hash cache
# (node_modules/.cache/audit-gate.json, 24h TTL) so commits that don't touch
# dependencies re-audit instantly; offline (registry unreachable) it only
# warns — the CI quality job re-checks on push.
# `git commit --no-verify` skips all of this in an emergency.
AUDIT_CACHE=1 AUDIT_SOFT_OFFLINE=1 node scripts/quality-chain.mjs lint test audit